<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmers wait for $4.00.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmers wait for $4.00.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were higher on Friday but movement remained very slow as farmers waited for $4.00 a bushel, several cash grain merchants said.</p>
<p>&quot;Futures were up and we raised our basis but there's still nothing moving,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said. &quot;We need to get back up over that $4.00 mark.&quot;</p>
<p>Some merchants expected movement to pick up next week as government wheat loans expired. Farmers have the option at expiry to leave the wheat under loan or redeem it and then sell it in the cash market.</p>
<p>&quot;The farmer has some loan wheat due on June 1 and he should be selling some of that,&quot; a Minnesota dealer said.  </p>
